WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.203
To understand the science, we
normally end up concentrating

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.472
on the stupid, but
every now and then,

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.707
we get the chance to
study at the feet,

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.477
or in this case, the
hands of a real expert.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.981
Meet Kevin from Switzerland.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.451
He's going to try and set a
Guinness World Record title

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.521
for the fastest
descent of 50 stairs

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.689
while walking on his hands.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.558
Good luck, Kevin.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.494
[music playing]

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.440
[cheering]

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:43.176
Wow, 14.58 seconds.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.377
I couldn't run it in that time.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.481
Don't forget, the problem
with walking on your hands

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.084
is there's nothing to
catch you when you fall,

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:54.888
and for most people,
falling is almost inevitable

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.891
[thud]

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.526
if you can get up
in the first place.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.063
Ah, that's much better.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.501
[thumping]

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.336
Yeah, really well.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.974
I would advise quite strongly
that you don't try this.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:18.378
The thing is Kevin knew science,
and when you know science,

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:20.647
it's just like a walk
in the park, only

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:24.184
upside down, on your hands,
and not necessarily in a park.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.588
First, he swings
his legs upwards,

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.757
generating just enough
angular momentum

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:33.793
to stay balanced upside down.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.831
His arms must be strong
enough to support his weight.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.967
Being upside down can be
disorienting as the vestibular

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:44.404
system located in the
inner ear sends signals

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:47.006
to the brain telling
him he's inverted,

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:50.910
meaning he must concentrate
more to stay oriented.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:54.481
Going downstairs, he generates
more angular momentum, which he

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.616
balances out by
going down quickly

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.452
and moving his arms,
his base of support

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:02.155
under his center of mass.

